// @run
// @log frb
// @hint redundant type annotation: `v` is inferred as `() => ({f: () => string} | null)[]`
// IT LOWERS NOW, AND THE REJECT THIS FILE PINNED IS RETIRED. A LAMBDA whose result is a
// ref-list of a NULLABLE struct with a CLOSURE-ONLY field
// (`() => ({f: () => string} | null)[]`) used to be a deferred rep composition that the
// emitter refused: `structElemFieldsPlain` admits a CLOSURE field, the element pinned
// through `nulStructElemListRetName`, and the nullable list-element lowering rejected
// cleanly with "a nullable-{…} list element has no rep; use a non-null element type" (was
// `cloCallReflistElemTwin`'s call-site floor before the closure-field admission — both
// clean loud REJECTs, never a trap).
//
// WHAT CHANGED: the shape interner's element comparison used to be a CONSTANT FALSE on
// five field codes (5/19/28/29/30 scored 0 matches in 1,365 corpus comparisons), because
// the row banked an ELEMENT name while the query held the whole composite TEXT. With the
// two sides asking `shapeFieldElemName` the same question, this element's shape dedups onto
// the row that already carries its rep instead of minting a second, un-repped one — so the
// composition resolves and lowers. Verified by running it, not by the absence of a
// diagnostic: it prints `frb`.
//
// The DIRECT array binding
// (`const v: ({f: () => string} | null)[] = […]`) lowers fully, and a nullable element
// struct with a MAP field beside the closure (`{a, f: {[string]: f64}, z: () => f64} | null`)
// now lowers fully too. rep-fuzz post-#1029, seed 361 case_00011 (multiobs leg p0r).
function go() {
  const v: () => ({f: () => string} | null)[] = () => ([{ f: () => ("frb") }])
  const t0 = v()[0]
  if (t0 != null) { print(t0.f()) } else { print("NULL") }
}
go()
